<main>
<h1>M2 · Cellular components of innate immunity</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Innate immunity lecture pack · EAACI/UEMS Knowledge Exam preparation</p>
<section class="objectives"><h2>After this module you can</h2><ul>
  <li>Place each innate cell on the myeloid or lymphoid branch of haematopoiesis and name its key growth factor.</li>
  <li>Compare neutrophils and macrophages, and describe classical (M1) and alternative (M2) macrophage activation.</li>
  <li>Distinguish conventional and plasmacytoid dendritic cells and explain how dendritic cells link innate and adaptive immunity.</li>
  <li>Explain "missing self" and the balance of activating and inhibitory receptors on natural killer (NK) cells.</li>
  <li>Compare mast cells, basophils and eosinophils (receptors, granules, mediators, disease relevance in allergy).</li>
  <li>Match ILC1, ILC2 and ILC3 to their transcription factors, cytokines and functions, and describe the role of ILC2s in allergy.</li>
</ul></section>

<dl class="abbr">
