</g>
<g><rect x="12" y="206" width="250" height="150" rx="8" fill="#f5f7fa" stroke="#6a4c93" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<rect x="12" y="206" width="250" height="30" rx="8" fill="#6a4c93"/><rect x="12" y="221" width="250" height="15" fill="#6a4c93"/>
<text x="22" y="227" class="t-head t-white">NK cell</text>
<text x="22" y="258" class="t-body">CD56+ CD3−; most CD16+</text>
<text x="22" y="278" class="t-body">Perforin + granzymes</text>
<text x="22" y="298" class="t-body">KIR, NKG2A, NKG2D, NCRs</text>
<text x="22" y="318" class="t-body">Kills infected/tumour cells</text>
<text x="22" y="338" class="t-body">Disease: GATA2, CD16, CHS</text>
</g>
<g><rect x="275" y="206" width="250" height="150" rx="8" fill="#f5f7fa" stroke="#c77d14" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<rect x="275" y="206" width="250" height="30" rx="8" fill="#c77d14"/><rect x="275" y="221" width="250" height="15" fill="#c77d14"/>
<text x="285" y="227" class="t-head t-white">Mast cell</text>
<text x="285" y="258" class="t-body">FcεRI high; c-KIT; MRGPRX2</text>
<text x="285" y="278" class="t-body">Histamine, heparin, tryptase</text>
<text x="285" y="298" class="t-body">Makes PGD2, LTC4, PAF</text>
<text x="285" y="318" class="t-body">Tissue-resident; weeks–months</text>
<text x="285" y="338" class="t-body">Disease: anaphylaxis, SM</text>
</g>
<g><rect x="538" y="206" width="250" height="150" rx="8" fill="#f5f7fa" stroke="#c77d14" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<rect x="538" y="206" width="250" height="30" rx="8" fill="#c77d14"/><rect x="538" y="221" width="250" height="15" fill="#c77d14"/>
<text x="548" y="227" class="t-head t-white">Basophil</text>
<text x="548" y="258" class="t-body">FcεRI high; IL-3</text>
<text x="548" y="278" class="t-body">Histamine, chondroitin sulfate</text>
<text x="548" y="298" class="t-body">Blood: &lt;1% of leukocytes</text>
<text x="548" y="318" class="t-body">Life span: days</text>
<text x="548" y="338" class="t-body">Recruited to inflamed sites</text>
</g>
<g><rect x="12" y="368" width="250" height="150" rx="8" fill="#f5f7fa" stroke="#b23a48" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<rect x="12" y="368" width="250" height="30" rx="8" fill="#b23a48"/><rect x="12" y="383" width="250" height="15" fill="#b23a48"/>
<text x="22" y="389" class="t-head t-white">Eosinophil</text>
<text x="22" y="420" class="t-body">IL-5R, CCR3; FcεRI very low</text>
<text x="22" y="440" class="t-body">MBP, ECP, eosinophil peroxidase</text>
<text x="22" y="460" class="t-body">Galectin-10 → Charcot-Leyden</text>
<text x="22" y="480" class="t-body">Anti-helminth; late phase</text>
<text x="22" y="500" class="t-body">Disease: allergic asthma</text>
</g>
<g><rect x="275" y="368" width="250" height="150" rx="8" fill="#f5f7fa" stroke="#6a4c93" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<rect x="275" y="368" width="250" height="30" rx="8" fill="#6a4c93"/><rect x="275" y="383" width="250" height="15" fill="#6a4c93"/>
<text x="285" y="389" class="t-head t-white">ILC1 · ILC2 · ILC3</text>
<text x="285" y="420" class="t-body">No TCR; mucosal tissues</text>
<text x="285" y="440" class="t-body">ILC1: T-BET → IFN-γ</text>
<text x="285" y="460" class="t-body">ILC2: GATA3 → IL-5, IL-13</text>
<text x="285" y="480" class="t-body">ILC3: RORγt → IL-17, IL-22</text>
<text x="285" y="500" class="t-body">ILC2 ← IL-25, IL-33, TSLP</text>
</g>
<g><rect x="538" y="368" width="250" height="150" rx="8" fill="#f5f7fa" stroke="#6a4c93" stroke-width="1.5"/>
<rect x="538" y="368" width="250" height="30" rx="8" fill="#6a4c93"/><rect x="538" y="383" width="250" height="15" fill="#6a4c93"/>
<text x="548" y="389" class="t-head t-white">Innate-like lymphocytes</text>
<text x="548" y="420" class="t-body">γδ T, iNKT, MAIT, B-1 cells</text>
<text x="548" y="440" class="t-body">Low-diversity TCR or BCR</text>
<text x="548" y="460" class="t-body">MAIT: riboflavin metabolites</text>
<text x="548" y="480" class="t-body">iNKT: glycolipid on CD1</text>
<text x="548" y="500" class="t-body">B-1: fast IgM, no T-cell help</text>
</g>
</svg>
<figcaption><b>D5.</b> Innate cell "ID cards". Each card lists markers or receptors, granules or products, main job and a key disease. SM = systemic mastocytosis; CHS = Chédiak-Higashi syndrome. Fact IDs M2-F017, M2-F016, M2-F015, M2-F020, M2-F018, M2-F105, M2-F106, M2-F025, M2-F032, M2-F028, M2-F029, M2-F030, M2-F027, M2-F009, M2-F035, M2-F034, M2-F036, M2-F060, M2-F043, M2-F046, M2-F054, M2-F050, M2-F051, M2-F045, M2-F061, M2-F062, M2-F067, M2-F064, M2-F075, M2-F072, M2-F077, M2-F073, M2-F065, M2-F066, M2-F079, M2-F012, M2-F083, M2-F088, M2-F090, M2-F085, M2-F086, M2-F087, M2-F091, M2-F092, M2-F094, M2-F095, M2-F100, M2-F101, M2-F102, M2-F104. <span class="src">Abbas p.15</span> <span class="src">Abbas p.21-23</span> <span class="src">Abbas p.82</span> <span class="src">Abbas p.467</span> <span class="src">Abbas p.473</span> <span class="src">Abbas p.81</span> <span class="src">Abbas p.85-86</span> <span class="src">Janeway p.119</span></figcaption>
</figure>

<section class="keypoints"><h2>5 key points</h2><ol>
  <li>All innate cells come from the HSC. Granulocytes, monocytes/macrophages, DCs and mast cells are myeloid; NK cells and ILCs are lymphoid. <span class="src" title="M2-F001,M2-F003,M2-F006">Abbas p.30; Abbas p.32</span></li>
  <li>Most tissue-resident macrophages come from fetal precursors. Classical (M1) activation kills microbes; alternative (M2) activation repairs tissue. <span class="src" title="M2-F022,M2-F028">Abbas p.15; Abbas p.19</span></li>
  <li>pDCs are the main source of type I IFN; cDC1s cross-present to CD8+ T cells; cDC2s present to CD4+ T cells. <span class="src" title="M2-F037,M2-F035,M2-F034">Abbas p.22; Abbas p.21-23; Abbas p.21</span></li>
  <li>NK cells kill when activating signals win. Loss of MHC-I ("missing self") removes the inhibition by KIRs and CD94/NKG2A. <span class="src" title="M2-F049,M2-F053,M2-F054">Abbas p.83; Abbas p.85</span></li>
  <li>Mast cells and basophils have high FcεRI; eosinophils have low FcεRI. ILC2s (GATA3; IL-5, IL-13) respond to IL-25, IL-33 and TSLP and start allergic inflammation early. <span class="src" title="M2-F067,M2-F094,M2-F098,M2-F099">Abbas p.466; Abbas p.81; Abbas p.94; Abbas p.465</span></li>
</ol></section>

<section class="traps"><h2>3 exam traps</h2><ol>
  <li>Tryptase, not histamine, is the mast cell activation marker: tryptase is in all human mast cells and no other known cell. Chymase is only in some mast cells. <span class="src" title="M2-F077,M2-F078">Abbas p.471; Abbas p.465</span></li>
  <li>CD16 on NK cells binds IgG (IgG1, IgG3), not IgE. The IgE receptors that trigger allergy are FcεRI on mast cells and basophils. <span class="src" title="M2-F052,M2-F067">Abbas p.84; Abbas p.466</span></li>
  <li>Follicular dendritic cells are stromal cells and do not present protein antigens to T cells. Do not confuse them with conventional DCs. <span class="src" title="M2-F040">Abbas p.22</span></li>
</ol></section>

<p class="related">Practice: <a href="../quiz/quiz.html#M2">M2 questions in the quiz</a> (IDs M2-A1 … M2-K2).</p>
